  "title": "Sanz Probable NDE 3561",
  "date": "1984",
  "content": "It was in the course of the surgical operation after the anesthesia, normally I shouldn't have felt anything. (Previously I already had four surgeries.) Suddenly I felt a very strong pain in the chest, as if my heart was taken off from my body and at the same time, a continuous sharp sound like a buzzer. Then the pain stopped as well as the sound, and I was sliding down a kind of black hall with a light at the bottom looking as a cotton material or steam appearance (difficult to describe). I didn't see any presences but heard voices as if several people were whispering together (male and female), 'Here she is coming, she is coming.' Suddenly another voice, a male voice, much louder and with an authoritarian tone said, 'No, it's too early.' That's it. When I woke up from my surgery, I was sick and my back was very painful. The day after the medic brought me to the exams room to have a long heart examination. The memory of my experience was very clear in my mind but I dared not tell people. I was afraid people thought I was crazy. Once I met a friend who told me that the phenomenon was well known. My experience is much shorter than the ones I read on the NDE sites but I can tell it still is very clear in my memory. I apologize for my English.",
